foundation.solution_text:
$f'(x) < 0$ means the curve is falling from left to right.
$f''(x) < 0$ means the curve is concave down, so the gradient becomes more and more negative.
The curve therefore falls, and falls ever more steeply: it is decreasing at an increasing rate.
